The synchronous reply path answers too, and that is what held MoneyMoney at its splash.

Patch 0003 gave xpc_connection_send_message_with_reply an answer when the service never resolved.
Its SYNCHRONOUS twin never got the same guard, and the omission is worse there: a caller that asked
for a synchronous reply has nowhere else to be. activateLocked releases both ports when the lookup
fails, so dispatch_mach_send_with_result_and_wait_for_reply waits on ports that can never carry a
reply, and it waits forever.

TRACED END TO END. MoneyMoney runs SecStaticCodeCheckValidity on a background thread while its main
thread keeps animating a spinner, so the process looks merely slow: window up, run loop turning,
nothing wrong on any log. With CIDER_TRACE_SECITEM the boundary speaks and the missing line is the
finding:

    CIDER_CSAPI  staticValidate call flags=0x0 req=no /Applications/MoneyMoney.app/...
    CIDER_CSSTEP registerStapledTicket call
    nothing, ever

The FIRST thing a static validation does is register a stapled notarization ticket, that goes to the
syspolicy service over xpc_connection_send_message_with_reply_sync, and we run no syspolicyd. So
every static validation in the system stopped on its first step.

MEASURED AFTER: registerStapledTicket back now appears and validation moves on to
staticValidateCore and validateNonResourceComponents, which is where it stops next.

--- a/src/connection.m
+++ b/src/connection.m
@@ -1096,6 +1096,19 @@
 	XPC_CLASS(dictionary)* result = nil;
 	mach_msg_header_t* header = NULL;
 
+	/* THE SAME GUARD AS THE ASYNC PATH, and its absence here is worse: a caller that asked for a
+	 * synchronous reply has nowhere else to be. activateLocked releases both ports when the
+	 * service never resolves, so the wait below is on ports that can never carry a reply and it
+	 * never ends.
+	 *
+	 * This is what held MoneyMoney at its splash. Code signing registers a stapled notarization
+	 * ticket before it validates anything, that goes to the syspolicy service over
+	 * xpc_connection_send_message_with_reply_sync, and we run no syspolicyd -- so the very first
+	 * step of every static validation waited forever. */
+	if (this->activation_failed) {
+		return XPC_ERROR_CONNECTION_INVALID;
+	}
+
